{number: 110}
{title: Higher Ground}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I'm [Ab] pressing on the [Db] upward [Ab] way,
New heights I'm gaining [Eb7] every day;
Still [Ab] praying as I'm [Db] onward [Ab] bound,
"Lord, plant my feet on [Eb7] higher [Ab] ground."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Lord, [Ab] lift me up and let me [Db] stand,
By faith, on [Ab] Canaan's table-[Eb7] land,
A [Ab] higher plane than I have [Db] found;
Lord, [Ab] plant my feet on [Eb7] higher [Ab] ground.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
My [Ab] heart has no de-[Db] sire to [Ab] stay
Where doubts arise and [Eb7] fears dismay;
Though [Ab] some may dwell where [Db] these a-[Ab] bound,
My prayer, my aim, is [Eb7] higher [Ab] ground.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I [Ab] want to live a-[Db] bove the [Ab] world,
Though Satan's darts at [Eb7] me are hurled;
For [Ab] faith has caught the [Db] joyful [Ab] sound,
The song of saints on [Eb7] higher [Ab] ground.
{end_of_verse}
